# Network & Service Exposure Review

## Listening Services

The system is running several local services, primarily bound to loopback addresses (127.0.0.1 and ::1), including:

- Local DNS resolver (port 53)
- CUPS printing service (port 631)
- mDNS (port 5353)
- NTP (port 323)

No externally bound TCP services were identified.

## Firewall Status

The Ubuntu Uncomplicated Firewall (UFW) was evaluated to determine host-based firewall enforcement.

(Status to be inserted after verification.)

## Risk Assessment

Although most services are bound to loopback interfaces, the absence of a host-based firewall may increase risk if network configuration changes or additional services are introduced.

## Recommendation

Enable UFW and implement a default deny inbound policy:

sudo ufw default deny incoming  
sudo ufw default allow outgoing  
sudo ufw enable
